class Employee:
    def __init__(self, name, pay_rate):
        self.name = name
        self.pay_rate = pay_rate
    def weekly_pay(self, hours):
        return self.pay_rate * hours
class Manager(Employee):
    def __init__(self, name, pay_rate, bonus):
        super().__init__(name, pay_rate)
        self.bonus = bonus
    def weekly_pay(self, hours):
        return super().weekly_pay(hours) + self.bonus
Inheritance: Manager reuses Employee's attributes and constructor via super(). Overriding/polymorphism: weekly_pay is redefined, and code can call weekly_pay on any employee object.

